From 108b09e0a670346f79ffd9e38d918eaa9d3951df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeong, Heon" <blmarket@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:03:22 -0700
Subject: Fix memory leak when drawing tree mode preview

window_tree_draw_session() and window_tree_draw_window() create a format
tree for each window or pane they put in the preview and never free it.
Every other format tree in the file is freed -- window_tree_draw_info()
frees the one it expands its lines with, and so do the three build
functions -- so only the two preview loops were missed.

The preview is drawn on every key that moves the selection, so this grows
for as long as tree mode is on screen, at one tree per previewed window
or pane per draw. A server driven with 40 send-keys into a tree mode
opened with -w exits under AddressSanitizer with

    Direct leak of 10080 byte(s) in 60 object(s) allocated from:
        #2 format_create format.c:4211
        #3 window_tree_draw_window window-tree.c:764
        #4 window_tree_draw window-tree.c:907
        #5 mode_tree_draw mode-tree.c:1026
        #6 window_tree_key window-tree.c:1559

and the same for window_tree_draw_session with -s. None with this
applied.

Applies to 3.7b at a different offset: the label and vline calls upstream
carry the grid cell and box-lines arguments 3.7b's do not, and the two
loops are otherwise the same.
---
 window-tree.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/window-tree.c b/window-tree.c
--- a/window-tree.c
+++ b/window-tree.c
@@ -551,6 +551,7 @@ window_tree_draw_session(struct window_tree_modedata *data, struct session *s,
 			}
 			free(label);
 		}
+		format_free(ft);
 
 		if (loop != end - 1) {
 			screen_write_cursormove(ctx, cx + offset + width, cy,
@@ -688,6 +689,7 @@ window_tree_draw_window(struct window_tree_modedata *data, struct session *s,
 			}
 			free(label);
 		}
+		format_free(ft);
 
 		if (loop != end - 1) {
 			screen_write_cursormove(ctx, cx + offset + width, cy,
